<!--
  Intentionally empty.

  ILRepack.Lib.MSBuild.Task ships an auto-imported target that merges every *.dll in the output
  directory. That double-merges our own output: MelonMCP.csproj already merges mcs.dll in an
  explicit step, and the package's pass would then re-merge the result with mcs.dll again,
  failing on every duplicated mcs type.

  The package's target only runs when this file does NOT exist, so shipping it empty disables the
  automatic behaviour while keeping our explicit merge.
-->
<Project />
